en to rebar._proc.reap_process_group (_proc.py:26) — killpg SIGTERM→grace→SIGKILL→bounded drain'","`os.killpg`, SIGTERM/SIGKILL signal delivery, and `start_new_session` process-group semantics are POSIX; `os.killpg` does not exist on Windows and Windows has no equivalent process-group kill via these signals.","Matrix cell: Platform and venue includes Windows."],"finding":"The new pandoc invocation path relies on POSIX-only process-group semantics — `subprocess.Popen(start_new_session=True)` plus `reap_process_group`'s `killpg` SIGTERM/SIGKILL — with no cross-platform accommodation stated for the Windows cell of the support matrix.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd365f015d45738cb","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — 'Hard timeout + process-group reaping'; Scope — 'own subprocess.Popen(start_new_session=True)'","norm_id":"nae3ff7861ebd8af7","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","scenarios":["Windows workstation/CI running a reconcile that renders a DC field: on a pandoc timeout, `reap_process_group` invoking `os.killpg` raises AttributeError/OSError (or no-ops), so instead of a clean segment-level verbatim fallback the caller sees an unhandled exception and/or the CPU-spinning pandoc grandchild is left orphaned — the exact hang the story sets out to prevent."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"yes","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact