"blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.6,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":[],"finding":"The batching mechanism does not specify how the landed per-unit code-fragment preservation guarantee (_render_unit / code_fragments, wiki_render.py:376-390, 266-288) is preserved when a maximal run of _RENDER units is rendered as ONE pandoc document, nor the fallback granularity when pandoc exits 0 but silently corrupts a code fragment (a 'preservation_failure' that is neither a timeout nor a non-zero exit).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f89ebf785a3beb677","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — 'Batch contiguous SAFE units'; Scope — wiki_render.py; AC line 2","norm_id":"n54bf2c24f3398281","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","scenarios":[],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"State that a batched run's output is still checked against the concatenated `code_fragments` of every _RENDER unit in the run, and that a preservation failure (like a timeout/non-zero exit) degrades that whole run's segment to verbatim Markdown with the segment-level fallback marker — or, if per-unit granularity must be retained, re-render the failed run unit-by-unit before falling back.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.3333,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"na","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Specify consumer-side handling of a non-positive `dc_pandoc_timeout_s` — mirror `_acli_call_timeout` by treating a value <= 0 as 'unset, use the 10s default' before passing it to `proc.communicate`, rather than letting `minimum=0.0` admit an instantly-timing-out 0.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.3067,"drop_reason":"novelty","evidence":["Plan: 'validator `_as_float(v, k, minimum=0.0)`'","Plan: 'enforces the wall-clock timeout caller-side via `proc.communicate(timeout=dc_pandoc_timeout_s)`'","Plan invokes the ACLI precedent: config key 'mirrors `reconciler.jira_cli_timeout`' and 'the `acli_subprocess.py` pattern'","acli_subprocess.py:89 `return value if value > 0 else _DEFAULT_ACLI_TIMEOUT`, docstring:80-81 'a zero/negative timeout would make communicate(timeout=0) time out every call instantly'","The fallback path is explicitly non-raising: plan 'degrade that entire segment to its original Markdown verbatim … without raising'"],"finding":"The timeout validator `_as_float(v, k, minimum=0.0)` admits an explicit 0, but the consumer enforces the timeout via `proc.communicate(timeout=dc_pandoc_timeout_s)`, so a configured 0 makes every render time out instantly and silently degrade ALL safe-run segments to verbatim Markdown — the exact hazard the ACLI precedent the plan invokes guards against by treating a non-positive value as 'unset, use default'.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f8e5a6a293e47316e","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope / config bullet: `validator _as_float(v, k, minimum=0.0)`; Approach (timeout via proc.communicate); AC line 1","norm_id":"nf57ee6c145f513b1","priority":0.2933,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["An operator sets reconciler.dc_pandoc_timeout_s=0 (e.g. intending 'disable the timeout'), and every safe-run render silently falls back to verbatim Markdown, dropping all wiki richness with no error surfaced."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Have the wiki_render consumer resolve the effective timeout as `value if value > 0 else 10.0` (the ACLI precedent at acli_subprocess.py:89), so an explicit 0 or negative value falls back to the default instead of timing out every render; keep the validator's `minimum=0.0` only if you additionally document that 0 means 'use default'.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Re-ground the 'persistent server out of scope' decision: check the pinned pypandoc-binary pandoc-cli for the `pandoc server` subcommand / `pandoc-server` symlink (and its compile-time server flag), not just for a `--server` flag in `--help`, and re-state why a persistent server is still out of scope on that correct basis.","cohort":["T1"],"criteria":["T1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.7,"drop_reason":"novelty","evidence":["Retrieved pandoc.org/pandoc-server.html and ANN pandoc 2.19.1 (Google Groups) / jgm/pandoc-server README: 'Starting with version 2.19.2, pandoc itself can be run as a full-featured server' — invoked via `pandoc server` (first argument) or symlink to `pandoc-server`, NOT a `--server` flag.","Retrieved Hackage pandoc-3.6.4 changelog: 'Add server flag to pandoc-cli, allowing it to be compiled without server support' — whether the bundled pypandoc-binary pandoc-cli shipped WITH server support is the real, unverified question.","The story's problem #1 is the per-field subprocess spawn tax; a persistent server would directly attack it, so the out-of-scope call is load-bearing on the performance thesis, not incidental."],"finding":"The plan's basis for ruling a persistent pandoc server out of scope — 'exposes no --server/daemon — verified absent from --help' — probes only the flag form; pandoc's server mode is actually invoked as the `pandoc server` subcommand or via a `pandoc-server` symlink (present since pandoc 2.19.x, i.e. before the pinned 3.6.1), so the capability assertion is under-grounded on a performance-relevant point.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa716901d41fc01fc","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — first bullet, parenthetical: 'The pinned wheel's pandoc 3.6.1 exposes no --server/daemon — verified absent from --help — so a persistent server is out of scope.'","norm_id":"n220e5cee728325c9","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["A reviewer or implementer checks the pinned wheel's binary for `pandoc server` / a pandoc-server symlink and finds server mode IS available, reopening a cheaper alternative to the batching-only approach.","The batching approach is built while a lower-spawn-cost server path was dismissed on an incorrect '--help' probe."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Replace the parenthetical with: verify via `pandoc server --help` (or presence of a `pandoc-server` symlink / the compile-time server flag) whether the pinned wheel's binary supports server mode; if it does not ship server support, cite that as the out-of-scope basis; if it does, add a one-line rationale for preferring per-run batching over a persistent server (e.g. process-isolation of pathological inputs per the timeout/reaping requirement).","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"64b2875b8ea281d5","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["0c2ec174c1ab7303",7946],"description_boxes":["0aad7da77d2ed59c",0],"file_impact":["f9576eec361ddb89",9],"ticket_id":["07b9e767e67baae5",19]},"metrics":{"cache_read_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"claim_path":"no-llm/no-netwo